# The eight-dimension design pass and its critique. Reference material for the
# implementation, superseded by CLAUDE.md and the approved plan wherever they
# disagree. Kept on disk, out of history: it is a megabyte of working notes.
.design/

# Local bundle cache written by `hexdocs prefetch` and `hexdocs build`.
.hexdocs-cache/

# The terraform stack's working files. `.terraform/` is a provider cache the aws provider
# alone makes 778 MB of; the tfvars carry the account id, the bucket name and the publisher
# map, and the state and plan files carry every rendered policy. None of them belongs in a
# public repository, and `scripts/check-infra.mjs` fails if git ever tracks one.
#
# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately absent from this list. It is committed, because
# `~> 6.0` floats and the lock file is what makes CI and a laptop verify the same provider.
#
# These globs are narrower than `FORBIDDEN_TRACKED` in `scripts/check-infra.mjs` on
# purpose, and they are not a copy of it. They cover the spellings an operator will really
# have at `infra/` top level; the guard's predicates are wider, so that the invariants row
# catches the shapes no glob here reaches, such as a `.tfstate` under `infra/tests/` or a
# `.terraform` directory nested below the top level. A belt that matched the braces exactly
# would catch nothing the braces missed.
infra/.terraform/
infra/*.tfvars
# Terraform auto-loads `terraform.tfvars.json` and `*.auto.tfvars.json` exactly as it loads
# their HCL twins, and `infra/*.tfvars` does not match either.
infra/*.tfvars.json
infra/*.tfstate
infra/*.tfstate.*
infra/*.tfplan
